# Emblem @VERSION@ - icons with default images and emblems

Emblem lets an icon borrow a shared default image (a drawer, a page) and
put an emblem on it: a small picture that says what is inside, like a
note for music or a globe for internet things. The emblem can get a soft
shadow or a glow, or be grayed, darkened or brightened.

It is an icon module for icon.library (`LIBS:IconModules`), so Workbench,
file managers and every other program that shows icons show the result.
Change one image in `ENVARC:sys/emblem` and every icon that uses it
changes with it. No patches.

Emblem is an [OpenAmiga.org project](http://openamiga.org/?function=gitproject&name=Emblem-icons).
The source code, test versions and bug reports are at
<https://github.com/OpenAmiga-org/Emblem-icons>.

## Features

- Default images and emblems as PNG files (any PNG; true colour with
  alpha is best), scaled to the size the setting asks for.
- Effects per layer: `SHADOW`, `GLOW`, `GRAY`, `DARK`, `BRIGHT`, `NONE`;
  a settings file chooses the effect for settings without one, and the
  shadow and glow look (offset, softness, opacity, colour).
- `INTERNAL`: an icon's own picture as the emblem (a program's picture
  on a drawer image).
- The icon's own pictures are always kept: saving never stores the
  composed picture, and converting back gives the original icon.
- New or changed images show on the next icon load, without a restart.
- Icons need the module's own file format; the `EmblemIcon` command
  converts icons to it and back and sets their settings, one by one, by
  pattern, or whole drawer trees.
- A small sample set (AmigaOS 4.1 icon style) for the ten example icons,
  and `RemoveSamples` to delete just those images.

## Installation

Unpack the archive and double-click `Install` in the `Emblem` drawer. It
installs, updates and removes everything (removing turns Emblem icons
back into normal ones).

After installing, restart the computer: icon.library loads icon modules
only when it starts.

## Contents

- `Libs/IconModules/emblem.iconmodule`: the icon module
- `C/EmblemIcon`: converts icons and sets their settings
- `Images/`: the sample images (go to `ENVARC:sys/emblem`)
- `Examples/`: ten example icons, one feature each, and a ReadMe
- `Emblem.guide`: the manual (AmigaGuide)
- `Emblem-format.txt`: the file format, for programmers
- `Install`, `RemoveSamples`, `LICENSE.txt`

## Using it

Four settings do it, kept in the icon file (not in its tool types, so
programs that read their tool types as arguments never see them):

    IMAGE=DrawerNS
    IMAGESELECTED=DrawerS
    EMBLEM=EmblemMusic,28,28,34,32,SHADOW
    EMBLEMSELECTED=EmblemMusic,28,28,34,32,SHADOW

`EmblemIcon` sets them, for example:

    EmblemIcon Work:Music SET="IMAGE=DrawerNS|EMBLEM=EmblemMusic,28,28,34,32"

`Emblem.guide` explains every setting, the effects and the settings file.

## License

Public domain (The Unlicense, see `LICENSE.txt`), the sample images and
icons too.

## History

### 1.1 (20.11.2026)

- The settings are kept in the icon file, no longer in the tool types
  (most Prefs editors refused to start with them); module 1.1,
  EmblemIcon 1.2 (SET, UNSET, TYPE); small sample set and RemoveSamples;
  new AmigaOS 4.1 style pictures for the package's icons and the sample
  set.

### 1.0 (15.11.2026)

- First release.
